---
import Base from '~/layouts/Base.astro'
import Prose from '~/components/Prose.astro'

// The privacy policy on Google's consent screen. Keep it in step with what
// convex/schema.ts stores.
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="What Tian stores, and where">
  <Prose>
    <h1>Privacy in Tian</h1>
    <p>
      Tian is a set of games for learning Mandarin, made by Gorm Rødder for
      family and friends. It has no advertising, no tracking and no analytics.
    </p>

    <h2>Without signing in</h2>
    <p>
      Your word bank, scores and settings are kept only in the browser on the
      device you use. None of it is sent to us, unless you turn on the daily
      reminder.
    </p>

    <h2>The daily reminder</h2>
    <p>
      If you turn on the reminder in Settings, we store, for that browser or
      phone:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        the address and keys its push service (Apple's, Google's or
        Mozilla's) gave it for notifications from Tian;
      </li>
      <li>the time you chose, and your time zone;</li>
      <li>
        the last day you finished Today's session, so that no reminder comes
        on a day you have done it;
      </li>
      <li>
        if you are signed in, which account it belongs to, so that a session
        finished on another of your devices counts too.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use this only to send the reminder, through that push service.
      Turning the reminder off deletes it. If you turn off notifications from
      Tian on the device instead, the push service tells us the address is no
      longer in use, and we delete it then.
    </p>

    <h2>When you sign in with Google</h2>
    <p>We then store:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        your name, email address and profile picture from Google, to know who
        is signed in;
      </li>
      <li>
        your word bank: the words you have met, your scores and progress.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We use this only to show you your progress on the devices where you are
      signed in. Gorm sees the names and email addresses of everyone who has
      signed in, and the first time you sign in, your name and email address
      are sent as a notification to Gorm's inbox on
      <a href="https://ymse.land">ymse.land</a>, which is also kept with
      Convex. We share nothing with anyone and use it for nothing else.
    </p>

    <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
    <p>
      With <a href="https://www.convex.dev">Convex</a>, which runs the
      database for us on servers in Northern Virginia, USA. The sign-in itself
      goes through Google. The page loads its fonts from Google Fonts and the
      stroke order of characters from jsDelivr, which, like any website, see
      your IP address.
    </p>

    <h2>Deletion</h2>
    <p>
      If you want your account and everything that belongs to it deleted,
      write to <a href="mailto:gorm@ymse.land">gorm@ymse.land</a>, and we will
      delete it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:gorm@ymse.land">gorm@ymse.land</a>.
    </p>
    <p><a href="/about">About Tian</a></p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
